# Normalise line endings in the repository rather than leaving it to each developer's
# core.autocrlf. Without this the bytes in a working tree depend on git configuration,
# which is invisible for ordinary source and decisive for a generated file compared byte
# for byte - see build/vsts-validate.ps1, which regenerates LicenseIdentifiers.json and
# fails the build if the committed copy differs.
* text=auto

# LF regardless of platform. The catalog above is generated by ConvertTo-Json, which
# emits CRLF on Windows and LF elsewhere; pinning the checkout is what stops "works
# here, fails in CI".
*.json text eol=lf
*.ps1 text
*.psm1 text
*.psd1 text
*.ps1xml text
*.cs text
*.md text
*.yml text

# Binary - never normalise, never diff as text.
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
